    "body": "Backport of a7d3835cb9f2 (vim-patch:9.2.0495, from #39842) to `release-0.12`.\n\nThe fix for CVE-2026-47162 / [GHSA-crm5-rh6j-2c7c](https://github.com/vim/vim/security/advisories/GHSA-crm5-rh6j-2c7c) landed on master in May, but #39842 wasn't labeled `ci:backport release-0.12`, so the backport bot never ran. As a result `release-0.12` and v0.12.5 still ship the vulnerable `s:NetrwBookHistSave()` line. That function writes directory names unescaped into `.netrwhist`, which netrw later `:source`s, so a directory name containing `'` can run Vimscript.\n\nConflicts were limited to context that differs on the release branch:\n- `netrw.vim`: kept the release branch's \"Last Change\" history and added one entry for this fix\n- `test_plugin_netrw.vim`: master has tests the release branch doesn't; this PR only adds `Test_netrw_injection` from the original commit\n\nThe functional change is the same one-line `string()` fix as on master.\n\ncc @zeertzjq @justinmk, since this is probably worth getting into 0.12.6.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-08T12:31:18Z",
